# Low Water, Act 1: the ruleset. Director's file. Private, 2026-10-16.
# Systems: design/SYSTEMS-FULL.md. Format: design/LWD1-FORMAT.md (draft 2, the engine's dialect).
# Keys the engine does not read yet are marked (R n) in design/NOTES-FOR-ENGINEER.md.

@rules
check-mode: fixed
xp-per-level: 1
points-per-level: 1
skill-cap: 4
creation-points: 11
attr-min: 1
attr-max: 5
cabinet-slots: 3
cabinet-slots-max: 6
forget-cost: 1
rep-min: -3
rep-max: 3
autosave-minutes: 10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- compartments
@attr pen
name: THE PEN
short: PEN
about: Reckoning. Sums, papers, memory, the scene put back together from what is left.

@attr coat
name: THE COAT
short: COAT
about: Bearing. The body in weather, on stairs, on wet stone; and the dignity of a dry coat.

@attr hat
name: THE HAT
short: HAT
about: Manner. What Lamb does with people, and what people do with Lamb.

@attr nose
name: THE NOSE
short: NOSE
about: Instinct. Smell, the dark, the hidden thing, and the sea in the joints.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the sixteen voices
@skill sum
name: SUM
attr: pen
about: Times, distances, clocks, money, counting. Distrusts every clock. Enjoys a remainder.

@skill precedent
name: PRECEDENT
attr: pen
about: Eleven years of claims, salvage law and the Shelf's practice. Always has a case number.

@skill smallprint
name: SMALL PRINT
attr: pen
about: Documents, signatures, clauses, ink. Delighted by a crossing-out.

@skill carbon
name: CARBON
attr: pen
about: Puts a scene back as it happened, from what is left. Speaks of the past in the present tense.

@skill knees
name: KNEES
attr: coat
about: Stairs, wading, distance. Complains, then does it.

@skill ballast
name: BALLAST
attr: coat
about: Footing and balance; steadiness when the ground or a person moves. Low, slow, nautical.

@skill pride
name: PRIDE
attr: coat
about: Composure, the dry coat, being taken seriously. Counts the years dry.

@skill grip
name: GRIP
attr: coat
about: Hands. Climbing, forcing, carrying, switches. Talks about what the hands feel.

@skill condolence
name: CONDOLENCE
attr: hat
about: Reading grief and pain, and letting people say what they lost. A little too sure it understands.

@skill formletter
name: FORM LETTER
attr: hat
about: Official manner, bluff, the guise kept up. Speaks in the passive voice, as letters do.

@skill chit
name: THE CHIT
attr: hat
about: Bargains, bribes, debts and what a thing is worth. A shopkeeper in the head.

@skill hearsay
name: HEARSAY
attr: hat
about: Planting, reading and steering rumour. Leans in. Has always just heard.

@skill smell
name: SMELL
attr: nose
about: Literal smell, and the Gut's language. Ecstatic and disgusting in equal measure.

@skill dark
name: THE DARK
attr: nose
about: Sight and hearing without light; what fear knows. Speaks more as Dread rises.

@skill undertow
name: UNDERTOW
attr: nose
about: What people hide, and the pull toward it. Persuasive. Never quite says what it wants.

@skill salt
name: SALT
attr: nose
about: The body's sense of tide and weather. Speaks as joints and skin.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the Kit (instruments as voices; condition is the base)
@skill candlemas
name: CANDLEMAS
base: 3
train: no
about: A brass photometer. Light, the kind of light, and the colour of a thing in it. Vain. Will not name a colour under sodium.

@skill glass
name: THE GLASS
base: 3
train: no
about: A pocket barometer. The weather an hour ahead, and how much the town knows of what Lamb has said. A gossip.

@skill almanac
name: THE ALMANAC
base: 4
train: no
about: A tide table with a brass dial. The tide now and for six hours. Precise, with a grudge against the moon.

@skill damp
name: THE DAMP
base: 2
train: no
about: A hair hygrometer, strung with the hair of Assessor Pollard, retired or deceased. Wetness, and how long ago. Melancholy.

@skill vane
name: THE VANE
base: 3
train: no
about: A tin cockerel on a folding stick. Wind, and where sound, smell, smoke and spray are carried. Excitable.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- environment and condition modifiers (SYSTEMS-FULL 2.1)
@modifier mod.sum.wear
skill: sum
mod: -1
when: meter.wear >= 6
why: Tired

@modifier mod.sum.desk
skill: sum, precedent
mod: 1
when: (at(office) | at(harbour) | at(room)) & light >= 0.3
why: A lit desk

@modifier mod.smallprint.dark
skill: smallprint
mod: -3
when: light < 0.15
why: Too dark to read

@modifier mod.carbon.place
skill: carbon
mod: 2
when: at(weigh_out) | at(lamproom) | at(drowned)
why: Where it happened

@modifier mod.carbon.washed
skill: carbon
mod: -2
when: clock >= 01:30 & (at(weigh_out) | at(drowned))
why: Rain and tide have been over it

@modifier mod.knees.cold
skill: knees
mod: -1
when: meter.cold >= 4
why: Cold

@modifier mod.knees.stairs
skill: knees
mod: -1
when: var.stairs_at > 0 & clock < var.stairs_at + 60
why: The 112 stairs, lately

@modifier mod.ballast.frost
skill: ballast
mod: -2
when: frost > 0 & (at(mole) | at(stairs) | at(quay) | at(steps))
why: Frost underfoot

@modifier mod.ballast.wet
skill: ballast
mod: -1
when: rain > 0.2 & !(at(brine) | at(room) | at(weigh_in) | at(harbour) | at(office))
why: Wet stone

@modifier mod.ballast.dark
skill: ballast
mod: -2
when: light < 0.05 & item.i.lantern == 0
why: Dark, no lantern

@modifier mod.pride.dry
skill: pride
mod: 1
when: wet < 0.1
why: Dry

@modifier mod.pride.wet
skill: pride
mod: -1
when: wet >= 0.3 & wet < 0.8
why: Wet

@modifier mod.pride.soaked
skill: pride
mod: -2
when: wet >= 0.8
why: Soaked

@modifier mod.grip.cold
skill: grip
mod: -2
when: meter.cold >= 6
why: Numb hands

@modifier mod.grip.rain
skill: grip
mod: -1
when: rain > 0.2 & !(at(brine) | at(room) | at(weigh_in) | at(harbour) | at(office) | at(hall) | at(smokehouse) | at(loft))
why: Rain on the hands

@modifier mod.condolence.fire
skill: condolence
mod: 1
when: at(brine) | at(room) | at(smokehouse)
why: By a fire

@modifier mod.condolence.sodium
skill: condolence
mod: -1
when: sodium > 0.6 & light >= 0.2
why: Faces will not read under sodium

@modifier mod.formletter.pride
skill: formletter
mod: 1
when: wet < 0.1
why: A dry coat speaks first

@modifier mod.chit.shelf
skill: chit
mod: -1
when: rumour(shelf.failed) > 0.5
why: The Shelf's name is worth less here

@modifier mod.hearsay.brine
skill: hearsay
mod: 1
when: at(brine)
why: The Brine

@modifier mod.smell.gut
skill: smell
mod: 2
when: indistrict(gut)
why: The Gut

@modifier mod.smell.rain
skill: smell
mod: -2
when: rain > 0.5 & !(at(brine) | at(room) | at(weigh_in) | at(harbour) | at(office) | at(hall) | at(smokehouse) | at(loft))
why: Rain

@modifier mod.smell.jar
skill: smell
mod: -3
when: worn(c.belljar)
why: A bell jar

@modifier mod.smell.blind
skill: smell
mod: 3
when: var.blindfolded == 1
why: Blindfolded

@modifier mod.dark.blackout
skill: dark
mod: 2
when: light < 0.05
why: Dark

@modifier mod.dark.lamp
skill: dark
mod: -1
when: light >= 0.3
why: Under a lamp

@modifier mod.dark.blind
skill: dark
mod: 2
when: var.blindfolded == 1
why: Blindfolded

@modifier mod.undertow.low
skill: undertow
mod: 1
when: tide < -0.2
why: Near low water

@modifier mod.undertow.high
skill: undertow
mod: -1
when: tide > 4.6
why: Near high water

@modifier mod.salt.soaked
skill: salt
mod: 1
when: wet >= 0.8
why: Soaked

@modifier mod.salt.floor
skill: salt
mod: 1
when: indistrict(floor)
why: On the floor of the sea

@modifier mod.candlemas.wind
skill: candlemas
mod: -2
when: wind.speed > 12 & item.fit.candlemas_shutter == 0
why: The wick gutters

@modifier mod.damp.saturated
skill: damp
mod: -9
when: var.damp_wet == 1
why: Saturated

@modifier mod.damp.keel
skill: damp
mod: -9
when: var.damp_hair == keel
why: Keel's hair reads everything as wet

@modifier mod.damp.wenna
skill: damp
mod: 2
when: var.damp_hair == wenna & (indistrict(mole))
why: Wenna's hair, on her stone

@modifier mod.damp.merrow
skill: damp
mod: 2
when: var.damp_hair == merrow & indistrict(floor)
why: Merrow's hair, on the mud

@modifier mod.damp.pip
skill: damp, salt
mod: 1
when: var.damp_hair == pip
why: Pip's hair feels the tide

@modifier mod.damp.lamb
skill: damp
mod: 2
when: var.damp_hair == lamb
why: Lamb's own hair

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- meters (R4: rise, full)
@meter cold
name: Cold
about: Wetness, wind and frost in the bones. Full: Lamb must shelter.
scope: global
min: 0
max: 10
start: 0
decay: 0
rise: 3 ? wet > 0.3
rise: 3 ? wet > 0.8
rise: 1 ? wind.speed > 9 & !(at(brine) | at(room) | at(weigh_in) | at(harbour) | at(office) | at(hall) | at(smokehouse) | at(loft))
rise: 1 ? frost > 0
rise: -12 ? stove
warn: 7 The cold has got into the pen hand.
full: chilled.$district

@meter wear
name: Wear
about: The hours of the night, bad light, stairs, strain. Full: Lamb nods off.
scope: global
min: 0
max: 10
start: 1
decay: 0
rise: 1 ? true
warn: 7 The Daybook's lines have begun to move about.
full: nod.$trait
after: 4
wait: 30

@meter dread
name: Dread
about: Blackout, being watched, the floor in fog. Full: the small thing.
scope: global
min: 0
max: 10
start: 0
decay: 1
rise: 2 ? light < 0.05
rise: 1 ? fog > 0.08 & indistrict(floor)
warn: 7 Something at the edge of the lamp has been patient for a while.
full: small.$district

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the Margin (inked notes are traits; their tide is the condition on each mod)
@trait m.clocks
name: Every Clock in Gullet Is Lying
about: The Brine's clock is slow, the ship's is fast, and the Board's is whatever the Board needs. Lamb keeps the true time in the margin.
research: 60
while: skill.sum -1
mod: skill.sum +2
do: set(margin.clocks)

@trait m.level
name: Water Finds Its Level
about: Once the water is over the boot it stops being an enemy and becomes a fact.
research: 45
while: skill.pride -1
mod: skill.knees +1 ? wet >= 0.3
mod: skill.salt +1 ? wet >= 0.3
mod: skill.pride -1

@trait m.owed
name: Everyone in Gullet Owes Somebody
about: The town runs on a slate. Find the chalk and you find the town.
research: 60
while: skill.hearsay -1
mod: skill.chit +2 ? at(brine) | indistrict(gut)

@trait m.flatfish
name: The Flatfish Position
about: Lie on the bottom, both eyes up, and say nothing. The water tells you more than the fish.
research: 30
while: skill.formletter -1
mod: skill.undertow +2 ? var.silent_scene == 1

@trait m.dark
name: The Town Is Honest in the Dark
about: Under the lamps Gullet performs. In the dark it only talks.
research: 90
while: skill.condolence -1
mod: skill.condolence +2 ? light < 0.1
mod: skill.formletter +2 ? light < 0.1
mod: skill.chit +2 ? light < 0.1
mod: skill.hearsay +2 ? light < 0.1

@trait m.colour
name: The Colour of a Thing
about: What a thing was in honest light it still is under the sodium. Lamb carries the colour in the margin.
research: 45
while: skill.condolence -1
mod: skill.candlemas +1
do: set(margin.colour)

@trait m.wet
name: Why Is He Wet
about: Nobody asks any more. Lamb asks, in pencil, every few minutes.
research: 180
mod: skill.dark +1
do: set(margin.wet)

@trait m.stairs
name: A Hundred and Twelve
about: Count them going up, and the counting carries you.
research: 30
while: skill.knees -1
mod: skill.knees +2 ? at(stairs) | at(lamproom) | at(gallery)
mod: skill.sum +1 ? at(stairs)

@trait m.copper
name: Copper Is a Better Citizen
about: Metal goes where it is useful and asks nobody's leave.
research: 60
while: skill.formletter -1
mod: skill.formletter -1
do: set(margin.copper)

@trait m.watched
name: Somebody Is Always Writing It Down
about: The brass poles, the open books. Lamb learns the feeling of a pencil moving in the next lamp.
research: 60
while: skill.dark -1
mod: skill.hearsay +1
do: set(margin.watched)

@trait m.pink
name: Pink Like a Cut
about: The lamps came back pink. Sodium does that for ten minutes when it starts cold. The pink is a clock.
research: 30
mod: skill.carbon +2 ? clock < 01:30
mod: skill.dark +1

@trait m.grace
name: Grace Is a Receipt
about: Somewhere behind every relic there is a sum, and someone who was paid it.
research: 60
while: skill.condolence -1
mod: skill.precedent +1

@trait m.pollard
name: Assessor Pollard's Hair
about: The Damp was a man once, and that man assessed this lamp twelve years ago.
research: 120
mod: skill.damp +1 ? var.damp_hair == pollard
mod: skill.precedent +1 ? var.damp_hair == pollard

@trait m.small
name: The Small Thing
about: Lamb saw it. It did nothing. That was the worst part, and also it was fine.
research: 60
while: skill.dark -1
mod: skill.dark +2
mod: skill.undertow +1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- precedents (character creation)
@archetype p.ledger
name: The Ledger Hand
about: 1180/P, the granary at Pell, where a clock stopped at the hour of the fire. 0441/R, the Rendle bank, whose ledger balanced too well. 2003/S, the Sallow ferry, and its timetable.
attr: pen 4
attr: coat 2
attr: hat 3
attr: nose 2
skill: sum 2
skill: precedent 2
skill: smallprint 2
skill: carbon 2
skill: condolence 1
skill: chit 1
trait: m.clocks
item: c.shelf_coat 1
item: c.shelf_hat 1
item: i.lantern 1
item: i.chits 6

@archetype p.wader
name: The Wader
about: 0907/M, the drowned choir at Mudlow. 1312/K, the Kettle Reach dyke. 1766/T, the tannery at Tull, assessed by smell.
attr: pen 2
attr: coat 4
attr: hat 2
attr: nose 3
skill: knees 2
skill: ballast 2
skill: pride 2
skill: grip 2
skill: salt 1
skill: smell 1
trait: m.level
item: c.shelf_coat 1
item: c.shelf_hat 1
item: i.lantern 1
item: i.chits 6

@archetype p.condoler
name: The Condoler
about: 2216/H, the glasshouses on Orrery Lane, hailed out. 0519/W, the Widow Arbery's roof, which she paid for twice. 1655/B, the bell at Brack, which fell on the man who rang it.
attr: pen 3
attr: coat 2
attr: hat 4
attr: nose 2
skill: condolence 2
skill: formletter 2
skill: chit 2
skill: hearsay 2
skill: precedent 1
skill: sum 1
trait: m.owed
item: c.shelf_coat 1
item: c.shelf_hat 1
item: i.lantern 1
item: i.chits 6

@archetype p.nightclerk
name: The Night Clerk
about: 2410/N, the bonded warehouse at Corve, watched from its own roof for three nights. 0388/L, the lighterman who was never on the manifest. 1907/E, the eel weir at Esk, assessed by ear.
attr: pen 2
attr: coat 2
attr: hat 2
attr: nose 5
skill: dark 2
skill: undertow 2
skill: smell 2
skill: salt 2
skill: hearsay 1
skill: formletter 1
trait: m.dark
item: c.shelf_coat 1
item: c.shelf_hat 1
item: i.lantern 1
item: i.chits 6

@archetype p.fitter
name: The Fitter
about: 1544/C, the clockwork crane at Coldharbour, mended to prove it had not been sabotaged. 2290/V, the Vellen sluice, opened with a spanner at three in the morning. 0612/D, the diving bell at Drem.
attr: pen 3
attr: coat 3
attr: hat 2
attr: nose 3
skill: grip 2
skill: sum 2
skill: carbon 2
skill: knees 2
skill: salt 1
skill: smallprint 1
trait: m.copper
item: c.shelf_coat 1
item: c.shelf_hat 1
item: i.lantern 1
item: i.chits 6
item: s.tin 1
item: s.cork 1

@var precedent
default: custom
values: ledger, wader, condoler, nightclerk, fitter, custom
about: Set by creation.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- clothing (R7: shed, warm, guise)
@item c.shelf_coat
name: The Shelf greatcoat
slot: coat
shed: 0.5
warm: 2
guise: shelf
mod: skill.pride +1 ? wet < 0.1
about: Shelf issue, eleven years dry until tonight.

@item c.shelf_hat
name: The Shelf bowler
slot: hat
shed: 0.3
guise: shelf
mod: skill.formletter +1
about: Hard, black, and taken seriously by people who have been sent letters.

@item c.oilskin
name: A borrowed oilskin
slot: coat
shed: 0.9
warm: 1
guise: floor
mod: skill.pride -1
about: From the Brine's peg. It smells of someone's uncle.

@item c.keeper_coat
name: Wenna's oxblood keeper's coat
slot: coat
shed: 0.6
warm: 2
guise: keeper
mod: skill.knees +1 ? at(stairs)
mod: skill.condolence +1 ? at(brine) | indistrict(mole)
about: Oxblood, which nobody on the quay has seen as oxblood for two years. She was never paid to wear it.

@item c.waders
name: Merrow's spare waders
slot: feet
guise: floor
mod: skill.ballast -1 ? !indistrict(floor)
about: Wading does not wet Lamb below the waist. On stone they slap.

@item c.blindfold
name: A Guild blindfold
slot: neck
guise: guild
about: Worn round the neck it says you have voted. Worn over the eyes it makes the nose an orator.

@item c.belljar
name: A Congregation bell jar
slot: hat
guise: pilgrim
mod: skill.smell -3
about: The breath fogs it. The world goes quiet and round.

@item c.lamplighter_coat
name: A Lamplighter's dark coat
slot: coat
shed: 0.6
warm: 2
guise: lamplighter
mod: skill.formletter +2 ? !indistrict(gut)
about: Constant Hobb's spare. The cuffs are polished by a brass pole.

@item c.mittens
name: Sabine's fingerless mittens
slot: hands
warm: 1
mod: skill.grip +1 ? meter.cold >= 4
about: Knitted from three colours of wool, which under sodium are one.

@item c.socks
name: Dry socks
stack: yes
about: Put on in the room above the Brine: wet feet reset, Cold falls by two.

@item c.keel_hat
name: The harbourmaster's hat
slot: hat
shed: 0
guise: board
mod: skill.pride -2
mod: skill.formletter +2 ? at(harbour) | at(quay)
about: It funnels water down the back of the neck by design, or by long habit.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- things carried and used
@item i.lantern
name: A storm lantern
slot: hand
mod: skill.ballast +1 ? light < 0.1
about: Light within its radius; reads colour; makes Lamb seen. A fill burns about half an hour.

@item i.paraffin
name: A fill of paraffin
stack: yes

@item i.egg
name: A pickled egg
stack: yes
about: Sabine's. A penny. Cold falls by one.

@item i.rum
name: Brine rum
stack: yes
about: Dread falls by three; the pen hand wanders for half an hour.

@item i.tea
name: Strong tea
stack: yes
about: Wear falls by two.

@item i.snuff
name: Shadwell's snuff
stack: yes
about: SMELL rises by two for half an hour, and so does everything else.

@item i.chits
name: Shelf chits
stack: yes
about: Expense vouchers. The town takes them at a rate that falls with the Shelf's name.

@item i.key_office
name: Keel's key
about: The weigh-house office. It is wet.

@item i.harbour_table
name: The Gullet harbour table
about: Printed for this harbour, this year. Exact heights for every step and gate.

@item i.prism_green
name: A green prism
about: Bottle glass, cast to the shape of one of Mother's prisms. Still warm, or was.

@item i.prism_113
name: Relic 113
about: A crown glass prism, sharp on every edge, numbered 113. Fennick wants it back.

@item i.copper_sack
name: Merrow's sack
about: Trust copper from the Old Light's lantern gear. Heavy as a verdict.

@item w.hammer
name: The weigh-house store hammer
slot: hand
about: A lump hammer, the head bound with wire.

@item i.orrin_letter
name: Orrin Teague's letter
about: Nine years old, addressed to someone in Hesk, never posted because the morning boat never suited.

@item i.hair
name: A hair in an envelope
stack: yes
about: Whose it is is written on the envelope.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- salvage pieces
@item s.brass
name: Brass
stack: yes

@item s.copper_wire
name: Copper wire
stack: yes

@item s.crown_glass
name: Crown glass
stack: yes

@item s.bottle_glass
name: Bottle glass
stack: yes

@item s.tin
name: Tin
stack: yes

@item s.wick
name: Wick
stack: yes

@item s.cork
name: Cork
stack: yes

@item s.mercury
name: A bead of mercury in a twist of paper
stack: yes

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- fittings (the Kit, fitted at the bench in the room above the Brine)
@item fit.candlemas_shutter
name: Candlemas: a smoked tin shutter
mod: skill.candlemas +1
about: The wick no longer gutters in wind.

@item fit.candlemas_eye
name: Candlemas: a crown glass eyepiece
mod: skill.candlemas +1
about: Reads a prism's number by the way it bends a light.

@item fit.glass_needle
name: The Glass: a new brass needle
mod: skill.glass +1

@item fit.almanac_table
name: The Almanac: the Gullet harbour table
mod: skill.almanac +1
about: Exact gate times in the Daybook.

@item fit.vane_tail
name: The Vane: a re-tinned tail
mod: skill.vane +1
about: No longer bends in a gust.

@recipe f.candlemas_shutter
name: Fit Candlemas with a shutter
in: s.tin 1
in: s.cork 1
out: fit.candlemas_shutter 1
when: at(room)
cost: 15

@recipe f.candlemas_eye
name: Fit Candlemas with a crown glass eyepiece
in: s.crown_glass 1
out: fit.candlemas_eye 1
when: at(room)
cost: 20

@recipe f.glass_needle
name: Give the Glass a new needle
in: s.brass 1
out: fit.glass_needle 1
when: at(room)
cost: 15

@recipe f.almanac_table
name: Paste the harbour table into the Almanac
in: i.harbour_table 1
out: fit.almanac_table 1
when: at(room)
cost: 10

@recipe f.vane_tail
name: Re-tin the Vane's tail
in: s.tin 1
out: fit.vane_tail 1
when: at(room)
cost: 10

# The Damp's hair is a scene, not a recipe: brine.lwd plays it (var damp_hair).
@var damp_hair
default: pollard
values: pollard, wenna, pip, merrow, keel, lamb

@var damp_wet
default: 0
about: 1 while the Damp is saturated (rain, wading); dried at a stove.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the Lamps of Gullet
@project l.steps_post
name: The paraffin post at the top of the steps
district: quay
stage: Leave from the Congregation | needs: | do: set(lamp.steps_post.leave) | about: It stands on the Congregation's steps. Fennick must allow it.
stage: Wick and fill | needs: s.wick 1, i.paraffin 1 | do: light(steps, 0.4, 0.3); set(lamp.steps_post.lit); quest(a1.lamps, first) | about: Colour reads at the top of the steps. The Lamplighters see the steps.

@project l.brine_porthole
name: The Brine's porthole lamp
district: brine
stage: Glass and collar | needs: s.bottle_glass 1, s.brass 1 | do: light(yard, 0.35, 0); set(lamp.porthole.lit); quest(a1.lamps, first) | about: The yard is lit. Nobody overhears in the yard except in fog.

@project l.gut_wires
name: The Gut's wire lamps
district: gut
stage: A steward's word | needs: | do: set(lamp.gut.leave) | about: Marrow's word, or Spratt's.
stage: Copper on the wires | needs: s.copper_wire 2 | do: light(gut, 0.45, 0); rep(guild, 1); set(lamp.gut.lit); quest(a1.lamps, first) | about: The Gut's lamps full; the gutter's colour shows.

@project l.balance
name: The lamp on the town balance
district: weigh
stage: Wick and fill, carried up | needs: s.wick 1, i.paraffin 1 | do: set(lamp.balance.lit); rep(board, -1); rep(guild, 1); quest(a1.lamps, first) | about: A light the whole quay can see that is nobody's but the town's.

@project l.drowned
name: A lantern in the drowned lamp
district: floor
stage: Leave a lantern | needs: i.lantern 1 | do: set(lamp.drowned.lit); rep(lowco, 2); quest(a1.lamps, first) | about: Hung in the hole of the Old Light before the water covers it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- factions (favour -3 to +3) and the Read
@faction board
name: The Harbour Board
about: Harbourmaster Keel, who is the Board.
start: 0
tier: -3 thinks you are a threat to the Board
tier: -1 thinks you are a nuisance
tier: 0 thinks you are a cheque in a coat
tier: 2 thinks you are an ally of the Board

@faction trust
name: The Trust, the Municipal and the Lamplighters
about: Alderman Crake's three hats, one address, one ledger.
start: 0
tier: -3 thinks you are an enemy of the town
tier: -1 is watching you
tier: 0 thinks you are an auditor
tier: 2 thinks you are useful

@faction guild
name: The Worshipful Guild of the Gut
about: Marrow Dunlin, steward; the vote in the dark.
start: 0
tier: -3 thinks you are an informer
tier: -1 does not like your smell
tier: 0 thinks you are a flatfish
tier: 2 thinks you are a nose, one of us

@faction congregation
name: The Congregation of the Filament
about: Deacon Fennick and forty in bell jars.
start: 0
tier: -3 thinks you are a thief of relics
tier: 0 thinks you are a pilgrim who has not yet seen
tier: 2 thinks you are a seer

@faction lowco
name: The Low Company
about: The salvors. Tub Merrow, Ferris Lugg, Nan Cockle.
start: -1
tier: -3 thinks you are the hangman
tier: -1 thinks you are the next person to hang them
tier: 1 thinks you are a witness
tier: 3 thinks you are one of them

@faction brine
name: The Brine
about: Sabine's neutral ground.
start: 0
tier: -3 thinks you are trouble
tier: 0 thinks you are a customer
tier: 2 thinks you are a regular

@faction shelf
name: The Mutual Indemnity of the Lower Shelf
about: By pneumatic tube, at intervals.
start: 0
tier: -2 thinks you are insubordinate
tier: -1 thinks you are delayed
tier: 0 thinks you are diligent

@var seenas_board
default: cheque
values: cheque, nuisance, threat, ally

@var seenas_trust
default: auditor
values: auditor, useful, enemy

@var seenas_guild
default: flatfish
values: flatfish, nose, informer

@var seenas_congregation
default: pilgrim
values: pilgrim, seer, thief

@var seenas_lowco
default: hangman
values: hangman, witness, ours

@var seenas_brine
default: customer
values: customer, regular, trouble

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- script state shared across districts
@var prov
default: none
values: none, wreckers, guild, trust, keeper, sea, refused
about: The provisional cause sent up the tube at midnight.

@var blindfolded
default: 0

@var silent_scene
default: 0
about: 1 for a scene in which Lamb has chosen silence (the Flatfish Position).

@var stairs_at
default: 0
about: Clock minute when Lamb last climbed the 112 stairs.

@var runs
default: 1
about: 1 when the engine plays Tide Runs; 0 plays each run's fallback check instead.

@var lens
default: whole
values: whole, saved, broken, green_broken

@var fish
default: stranded
values: stranded, turned, gulls, eaten

@var copper
default: none
values: none, hidden, returned, reported

@var tab_dilly
default: 0
@var tab_orrin
default: 0
@var tab_hobb
default: 0
@var tab_pip
default: 0
@var tab_cockle
default: 0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- quests
@quest a1.claim
name: Claim 4471/G
about: The Board's claim: darkness, malicious, telegraphed three hours before the dark.
stage: open: Find the cause of the loss before the tube takes it at ten past six.
stage: mechanism: The quay switch went down at 21:38 and Mother went with it. Why was she on it?
stage: wiring: Seven months ago Mother was moved onto the quay board. Signed Keel, approved Crake.
stage: restrike: She needs a hand at the panel after any loss of supply. Nobody's hand was there.
stage: foreknown: The claim was sent at 18:30. Someone knew the vote would darken her.
stage: glass: A third of the lens is green bottle glass. The Board wants a new lens. Why?
stage: light: The ferry was turned by a light in the drowned lamp.
stage: provisional: A provisional cause has gone up the tube. The town has heard it.
stage: cause: The cause has gone up the tube at dawn.
done: cause

@quest a1.lowlight
name: The Low Light
about: What burned in the drowned lamp at 22:20.
stage: seen: From the deck: a low light in the Old Light, and the helm going over. The ship's clock said 22:24.
stage: merrow: Merrow hung his lantern in the hole. He says it was out from 22:18 to 22:25.
stage: gap: The ferry turned at 22:20. For five minutes nothing of Merrow's was burning.

@quest a1.stairs
name: A Hundred and Twelve Stairs
about: Mother is dark. Somebody must climb.
stage: asked: Asked Wenna to climb to Mother.
stage: refused: Wenna will not climb.
stage: climbing: Wenna is climbing.
stage: burning: Mother is burning again, by Wenna's hand.
stage: alone: Mother is burning again, by Lamb's hand.
stage: dark: The second blackout put her out again.
done: burning, alone

@quest a1.nose
name: Lights Out for the Nose
about: The Guild's switch, and Marrow's guess.
stage: heard: The Guild votes in the dark. Someone must make it dark.
stage: scales: Fish scales on the switch handle.
stage: admitted: Marrow pulled the switch at 21:38 and put it back at 21:52.
stage: kept: Marrow's secret is kept.
done: admitted, kept

@quest a1.splinters
name: Splinters of the Eye
about: The Congregation's relics.
stage: relic: Fennick keeps splinters of the Eye.
stage: numbered: Relic 113 is a numbered crown glass prism, sharp on every edge. One of Mother's.
stage: bought: Fennick paid for them.

@quest a1.slate
name: The Slate
about: Sabine's chalk, the slow clock and the oven.
stage: tab: Wenna's mark on the tab at 21:45 and 22:10.
stage: oven: Green glass in the bread oven.
stage: wiped: Sabine wiped Lamb's slate.
done: oven

@quest a1.copper
name: Copper Doesn't Care
about: Merrow's sack of Trust copper.
stage: sack: Merrow's sack is under the settle by the Brine's stove.
stage: hidden: Lamb hid the sack.
stage: returned: Lamb gave the sack to the Lamplighters.
stage: reported: Lamb reported the sack to the Shelf.
done: hidden, returned, reported

@quest a1.tube
name: Tube Minded
about: Pip, the tube and a typewriter with a sticking e.
stage: tube: The Shelf answers by pneumatic tube, in the weigh-house.
stage: e: The Shelf's machine has a sticking e.

@quest a1.fish
name: Claim on a Fish
about: A fish the size of a cart on the harbour floor, claimed three ways.
stage: met: A fish, stranded, the size of a cart.
stage: claims: The Guild, the Low Company and the Congregation each claim it.
stage: turned: The fish is back in the channel.
stage: gulls: The gulls have the fish.
stage: eaten: The Guild has the fish.
done: turned, gulls, eaten

@quest a1.hair
name: The Damp's Hair
about: The Damp would like to be someone else.
stage: asked: The Damp asked for a new hair.
stage: rehaired: The Damp has a new hair.
done: rehaired

@quest a1.book
name: Gorm's Book
about: What the Lamplighters write about Lamb.
stage: noticed: Sergeant Gorm writes down who Lamb talks to.
stage: page: Lamb has seen a page of Gorm's book.

@quest a1.minutes
name: Eleven Minutes
about: The Brine's clock is eleven minutes slow.
stage: slow: The Brine's clock is eleven minutes slow. Sabine knows.
stage: jory: Jory Brine went out on the floor nineteen Low Nights ago, eleven minutes late.
stage: set: Lamb set the clock right.
stage: left: Lamb left the clock as it is.
done: set, left

@quest a1.vote
name: The Fish of the Year
about: The Guild's vote by smell.
stage: pans: Two fish on the voting pans. The strike carried by a nose.
stage: older: One of the fish was a day older than it should be.
stage: soot: Shadwell's soot dates its smoking: yesterday.
stage: spratt: Agnes Spratt swapped it, to lose the strike. It carried anyway.
done: spratt

@quest a1.frost
name: Frost
about: Who climbs to Mother before dawn, and what the frost keeps.
stage: hammer: Keel took the store hammer at a quarter past four.
stage: prints: Frozen drips on the 112 stairs, one per step, up and down.
stage: met: Lamb met Keel in the lamp room.
stage: saved: The lens is whole.
stage: broken: The lens is broken.
stage: green: Keel broke only the green rings. The evidence is gone; the light is honest.
done: saved, broken, green

@quest a1.room
name: The Room Above the Brine
about: Lamb's lodging.
stage: let: Sabine has let Lamb the room above the bar.
stage: wall: Something is pinned to the wall.

@quest a1.lamps
name: The Lamps of Gullet
about: The town's lights, which can be lit, mended or left.
stage: first: A lamp of Gullet burns because of Lamb.
stage: three: Three lamps of Gullet burn because of Lamb.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the Kit's readings (instrument keys as in the prototype: T G V C H)
@instrument almanac
name: THE ALMANAC
key: KeyT
about: The tide now, and the gates.
say: {{tide}} metres and falling. The floor is open to the gully. Low water at two minutes to eleven; the moon is responsible and absent. {when: clock < 22:58 & tide < -0.27}
say: {{tide}} metres. Slack. The sea is deciding, and it has decided. {when: clock >= 22:58 & clock < 23:12}
say: {{tide}} metres and rising. The gully shuts at 23:42, the lowest steps at 23:48, the drowned lamp at 23:52. I do not negotiate. {when: clock >= 23:12 & clock < 23:52}
say: {{tide}} metres and rising. The floor is closed. High water ten past five, five metres thirty. {when: clock >= 23:52 & clock < 05:10}
say: {{tide}} metres. High water. The quay's edge is the sea's edge. {when: clock >= 05:10 & clock < 05:30}
say: {{tide}} metres and falling. Nothing opens before dawn. {when: clock >= 05:30}

@instrument glass
name: THE GLASS
key: KeyG
about: Pressure and its trend; and what the town has heard.
say: Steady, darling. Falling a hair. Fog within the hour, if I know anything, and I know everything. {when: clock < 23:20}
say: Falling. Rain by twenty to midnight and the wind round to the south-west. Somebody is about to say something they can't take back. {when: clock >= 23:20 & clock < 23:35}
say: Low and falling. Heavier rain after one. The town is talking about you, a little. {when: clock >= 23:35 & clock < 01:30 & !(var.prov != none)}
say: Low. The whole quay has your midnight word in its mouth, darling, and is chewing. {when: clock >= 00:00 & clock < 04:10 & var.prov != none}
say: Rising, fast. Clear by ten past four, and cold behind it. Frost. Everything will hold its shape. {when: clock >= 01:30 & clock < 04:10}
say: High and rising. Clear, still, cold. Dawn will be pitiless. {when: clock >= 04:10}

@instrument vane
name: THE VANE
key: KeyV
about: The wind, and where it carries.
say: West! West, six metres! Everything said on this quay goes east. Mind your mouth on the windward side! {when: clock < 23:35}
say: South-west! Round she comes, nine metres, wet! Rain under every eave on the north-east faces! {when: clock >= 23:35 & clock < 04:10}
say: Nothing! Barely nothing! North-west and faint! Every word carries straight up and freezes! {when: clock >= 04:10}

@instrument candlemas
name: CANDLEMAS
key: KeyC
about: The light, its kind and the colour of a thing in it.
say: Nothing. You are standing in nothing. I am a photometer, not a medium. {when: light < 0.03}
say: Sodium. One line of the spectrum, the orange one. I will not be party to that orange. Ask me again in honest light. {when: sodium > 0.6 & light >= 0.03}
say: Paraffin. Warm, smoky, true. Colours read here. Show me a thing and I will tell you what it is wearing. {when: sodium <= 0.6 & light >= 0.2}
say: Carried light, or very little. Hold your lantern nearer, and nearer, and that is enough. {when: sodium <= 0.6 & light < 0.2 & light >= 0.03}

@instrument damp
name: THE DAMP
key: KeyH
about: Wetness, and how long ago.
say: Saturated. I can read nothing. I was a man's hair once and he was never dry either. Dry me at a stove. {when: var.damp_wet == 1}
say: Wet. Everything here is wet. You are {{wet}} parts in one wet, which is a fact, not a judgement. {when: var.damp_wet != 1 & wet >= 0.3}
say: Damp, at worst. The air is ninety parts in a hundred water. You are holding up, for now. {when: var.damp_wet != 1 & wet < 0.3}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- characters
@char wenna
name: Wenna Tallow
speaker: WENNA
faction: brine
about: Keeper of Mother, thirty-one years, the last six unpaid.
walkaway: That's right. Go and count something.
walkaway: I'll be on the stairs, if anybody wants me. Nobody does.
interrupted: Later. She's tripping.
fightstart: Not in my lamp room.

@char keel
name: Absalom Keel
speaker: KEEL
faction: board
about: Harbourmaster. Wet for eleven years.
walkaway: The Board will note the assessor's departure.
interrupted: The Board will finish that sentence another time.
fightstart: The Board did not want this.

@char crake
name: Ottilie Crake
speaker: CRAKE
faction: trust
about: Alderman; the Trust and the Municipal.
walkaway: Go, then. You know the way out; you knew the way in.
interrupted: Forgive me. Another time.
fightstart: Mrs Pellow. The constable, please.

@char marrow
name: Marrow Dunlin
speaker: MARROW
faction: guild
about: Shop steward of the Guild of the Gut.
walkaway: Swim off, flatfish.
interrupted: Hold your tongue a minute.
fightstart: Out of my hall, then, the hard way.

@char fennick
name: Ambrose Fennick
speaker: FENNICK
faction: congregation
about: Deacon of the Congregation of the Filament.
walkaway: Go with whatever grace you have.
interrupted: Wait. Listen. No. Go on.
fightstart: The jars, brothers. Mind the jars.

@char sabine
name: Sabine Brine
speaker: SABINE
faction: brine
about: Landlady of the Brine.
walkaway: Tab's open, love. It's always open.
interrupted: Hold that thought. Hold it, I said.
fightstart: Not on my floor. Out in the yard with it.

@char merrow
name: Tobias "Tub" Merrow
speaker: MERROW
faction: lowco
about: Master of the Low Company.
walkaway: Go on, then.
interrupted: Later.
fightstart: That's done it.

@char pip
name: Pip Gannet
speaker: PIP
faction: brine
about: Pot girl; minds the tube.
walkaway: Fine. I'll tell the tube you said goodbye.
interrupted: Hang on. Hang on, it's ringing.
fightstart: Shelf! Behind you!

@char gorm
name: Ida Gorm
speaker: GORM
faction: trust
about: Sergeant of the Lamplighters. Speaks only in questions.
walkaway: Written down: the assessor left. Would you like a copy?
interrupted: Would you hold that? Would you?
fightstart: Poles. Both ends. Would you mind?

@char hobb
name: Constant Hobb
speaker: HOBB
faction: trust
about: The youngest Lamplighter. Afraid of the dark. Carries two lanterns.
walkaway: Right. I'll put you down as going.
interrupted: Sorry. I've to see to the board.
fightstart: I'm not to fight the Shelf. I'm not to.

@char spratt
name: Agnes Spratt
speaker: SPRATT
faction: guild
about: Eel-wife. Voted against the strike. Wants to be steward.
walkaway: Off you go. The eels won't miss you.
interrupted: Wait. Something's burning.
fightstart: Knives, girls. The Shelf's asked for it.

@char mab
name: Mab Whelk
speaker: MAB
faction: guild
about: Gutter. Twin of Noll. Finishes his sentences, and disagrees with the ending.

@char noll
name: Noll Whelk
speaker: NOLL
faction: guild
about: Gutter. Twin of Mab.

@char shadwell
name: Ned Shadwell
speaker: SHADWELL
faction: guild
about: Smokehouse master. Reads time by soot.

@char gauze
name: Sister Gauze
speaker: GAUZE
faction: congregation
about: Has worn her bell jar for eleven years.

@char tobit
name: Tobit Quill
speaker: TOBIT
faction: congregation
about: Choirboy, nine. Sings the sodium restart as a hymn.

@char lugg
name: Ferris Lugg
speaker: LUGG
faction: lowco
about: Merrow's partner. Very tall. Never speaks above a whisper.
walkaway: Gone, then.
interrupted: Later.
fightstart: Right.

@char cockle
name: Nan Cockle
speaker: COCKLE
faction: lowco
about: Eighty-one. Walked to the Old Light as a girl, when it still had a door.
walkaway: Mind the tide on your way, it doesn't mind you.
interrupted: Shush. Listen to the water.
fightstart: I've still a good arm, mind.

@char penhallow
name: Ysolde Penhallow
speaker: PENHALLOW
faction: shelf
about: Master of the ferry Saint Cuthwin. Put the helm over at 22:20.

@char teague
name: Orrin Teague
speaker: TEAGUE
faction: brine
about: Has waited at the Brine for the morning boat for nine years.

@char dilly
name: Dilly Rudd
speaker: DILLY
faction: lowco
about: Floor child. Runs a book on whether the fish lives.

@char fewell
name: Lamplighter Fewell
speaker: FEWELL
faction: trust

@char bright
name: Lamplighter Bright
speaker: BRIGHT
faction: trust

@char strand
name: Lamplighter Strand
speaker: STRAND
faction: trust

@char coe
name: Lamplighter Coe
speaker: COE
faction: trust

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Margin notes earned by fighting (SYSTEMS-FULL 18.10)
@trait m.body
name: A Body Is Also Evidence
about: A bruise has a time on it, like ink. Lamb reads a fight afterwards the way Lamb reads a room.
research: 45
while: skill.condolence -1
mod: skill.carbon +2 ? var.fights > 0

@trait m.poles
name: The Pole Has Two Ends
about: Whoever holds the brass end is holding the other end too.
research: 45
while: skill.formletter -1
mod: skill.ballast +1 ? indistrict(quay) | indistrict(weigh)

@trait m.downwind
name: Downwind
about: In the Gut they find you by your smell. Keep the wind in your face and you are nobody.
research: 30
while: skill.hearsay -1
mod: skill.smell +2 ? indistrict(gut)

@var fights
default: 0
about: How many fights Lamb has been in tonight. The combat layer adds one per encounter.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the rework (REWORK-PLAN.md)
@var act2_strippers
default: town
values: town
about: Who strips the stranded ships at the second low water: the town's own people (decided 2026-10-17; the Hesk branch was removed).

@var appt
default: none
values: none, cells, vote, search, oven, keel
about: What the town has planned for the 02:50 blackout, set from the provisional cause (REWORK-PLAN 1.3).

@item i.rope
name: A coil of rope
about: For a hand line on the gully, a bar on a door, or the legs of someone running.

@item i.salt
name: A sack of salt from the Gut
about: For a frozen step, or a fish.
